      "title": "Assistant Professor of Communication Studies (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Communication Studies (Tenure-Track) - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant Professor of Communication Studies (Tenure-Track) - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Communication Studies (Tenure-Track) 497157 Full-Time Arts & Communication Department : Arts & Communication Salary : This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Description : Assistant Professor of Communication Studies (Tenure-Track) Position Title Assistant Professor of Communication Studies (Tenure-Track) Department of Arts and Communication, College of Humanities and Social Sciences, University of Houston-Downtown Start Date: Fall 2027 Position Description The Department of Arts and Communication at the University of Houston-Downtown in the College of Humanities and Social Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Communication Studies position. The appointment begins in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate expertise in one or more of the following areas: media studies or media production, corporate or organizational communication, strategic communication, public relations, digital communication, or related fields. They will contribute to a dynamic Bachelor of Arts in Communication Studies program and Master of Arts in Strategic Communication program. Responsibilities include teaching a 4-3 course load over the two long semesters in a variety of modalities including undergraduate and graduate communication courses; maintaining an active program of scholarly research and publication; participating in curriculum development and assessment; advising and mentoring students; and contributing to departmental, college, university, and professional service activities. Required Qualifications Earned Ph.D. in Communication Studies, Media Studies, Organizational Communication, Strategic Communication, Public Relations, or a closely related field from an accredited institution by the date of appointment. Expertise in one or more of the following areas: media studies or media production, corporate or organizational communication, strategic communication, public relations, digital communication, or related fields. Demonstrated evidence of effective teaching or strong potential for teaching excellence at the collegiate level. Evidence of an active or developing research agenda. Commitment to student success and engagement in a dynamic urban university environment. Preferred Qualifications Ability to teach across multiple areas of the Communication Studies curriculum. Experience teaching online, hybrid, and face-to-face courses. Evidence of community-engaged teaching, or experiential learning initiatives. Experience incorporating emerging communication technologies into teaching and research. Relevant professional experience in communication-related industries. About UHD The University of Houston-Downtown is a comprehensive public university and a constituent institution of the University of Houston System. UHD is designated as both a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) and a Minority-Serving Institution (MSI) and is committed to providing a student-centered education that prepares learners for professional success and civic engagement. Application Process Applicants should submit the following materials: Cover letter addressing qualifications for the position Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research agenda Unofficial graduate transcripts Three letters of recommendation Review of applications will begin on November 23, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) d5eab503 Last Name (required) 4484964b Email (required) 765dc97c Cell number 4e4113b4 244