      "title": "Adjunct, Arts and Communication, Communication Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct, Arts and Communication, Communication Studies - Houston, Texas, United States Adjunct, Arts and Communication, Communication Studies - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct, Arts and Communication, Communication Studies 496935 Part-Time Arts & Communication Adjunct, Communication Studies Job Description: The University of Houston-Downtown Department of Arts and Communication seeks qualified and committed instructors for the position of Adjunct Faculty in Communication Studies. We seek professionals that can serve as a generalist of communication studies with the ability to teach a wide breadth of communication studies courses. Successful candidates will be able to teach core courses such as Introduction to Communication and Public Speaking as well contribute to one or more of our concentration areas: media and public communication, health and relational communication, or organizational communication. Teaching opportunities will be offered in-person, hybrid, and/or fully online. Adjunct faculty should expect to be asked to teach on campus up to two-times per week and will be offered online opportunities as they are available. For online teaching, experience teaching in Canvas LMS is advantageous. Adjunct faculty are eligible for benefits if they teach three or more 16-week sections in a semester. Required Qualifications: MA in Communication Studies or related discipline College-level teaching experience Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Communication Studies or related discipline To apply, candidates must submit a resume or curriculum vita and a cover letter. Official transcripts and two signed letters of reference on academic letterhead will be required from candidates who reach the final stage of hiring consideration, but these documents are not needed in the initial application. The Department Chair will inform candidates about how and when to submit their transcripts and letters of reference. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are an Equal Opportunity Institution. Apply now First Name (required) ce1c4a35 Last Name (required) 0e2d9cc5 Email (required) 4590d85b Cell number 6e88f815 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) Côte d’Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Curaçao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (+253) Dominica (+1) Dominican Republic (+1) Ecuador (+593) Egypt (+20) El Salvador (+503) Equatorial Guinea (+240) Eritrea (+291) Estonia (+372) Eswatini (+268) Ethiopia (+251) Falkland Islands (Islas Malvinas) (+500) Faroe Islands (+298) Fiji (+679) Finland (+358) France (+33) French Guiana (+594) French Polynesia (+689) Gabon (+241) Gambia (+220) Georgia (+995) Germany (+49) Ghana (+233) Gibraltar (+350) Greece (+30) Greenland (+299) Grenada (+1) Guadeloupe (+590) Guam (+1) Guatemala (+502) Guernsey (+44) Guinea (+224) Guinea-Bissau (+245) Guyana (+592) Haiti (+509) Honduras (+