      "title": "Adjunct, English",
      "description": "Adjunct, English - Houston, Texas, United States Adjunct, English - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct, English 496319 Part-Time Closing on: Jun 7 2027 English Department: English Salary: Commensurate with Experience/Education Description: The University of Houston-Downtown (UHD) Department of English seeks qualified and committed instructors for the position of Adjunct Faculty in our First-Year Composition (FYC) or Technical Communication (TC) programs. Depending on experience and departmental needs, hired instructors will teach one of the following schedules: Two or more in-person sections of ENG 1301: Composition I and/or ENG 1302: Composition II throughout a 16-week fall/spring semester Two or more in-person or online sections of TCOM 3302: Business and Technical Writing throughout a 16-week fall/spring semester Adjunct faculty are eligible for benefits if they teach three or more 16-week sections in a semester. About University of Houston Downtown The second-largest university in Houston, the University of Houston-Downtown (UHD) is a comprehensive, four-year, urban university in the heart of downtown. UHD is a community of diverse faculty, staff, students, and regional partners dedicated to nurturing talent, generating knowledge, and driving socioeconomic mobility for a just and sustainable future. UHD is recognized as a Hispanic-Serving Institution and a Minority-Serving Institution. While the student population is largely Hispanic and African American, more than 64 countries are represented. Furthermore, UHD has the most affordable tuition among four-year universities in Houston, and 70% of its first-year students are the first in their families to attend college. Required Qualifications: ENG 1300, 1301, and/or 1302: PhD or MA in English (or directly related discipline) TCOM 3302: PhD or MA in Technical Communication (or directly related discipline) Preferred Qualifications: • ENG 1300-1301 (corequisite): Experience teaching college-level developmental English courses as instructor of record • ENG 1301 and/or 1302: Experience teaching college-level FYC courses as instructor of record • TCOM 3302: Experience teaching college-level professional/technical writing courses as instructor of record To apply, candidates must submit a resume or curriculum vitae and a cover letter. Official transcripts and two signed letters of reference on academic letterhead will be required from candidates who reach the final stage of hiring consideration, but these documents are not needed in the initial application. The departmental Assistant Chair will inform candidates about how and when to submit their transcripts and letters of reference. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 0dc52245 Last Name (required) b291338d Email (required) 8d90fadc Cell number c41f8ef0 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzavil