      "title": "Adjunct Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct Psychology - Houston, Texas, United States Adjunct Psychology - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Psychology 495611 Part-Time Psychology Department : Psychology Salary : Description : Adjunct positions in the Department of Psychology are filled as needed. To be considered a candidate for this position, please complete an on-line application. Also, please send an email, indicating your interest and qualifications, with attached curriculum vitae, to: Dr. Ruth Johnson, Assistant Chair of Psychology, johnsonru@uhd.edu . The Department of Psychology at the University of Houston-Downtown seeks qualified adjunct instructors for in-person and hybrid classes in psychology. The candidate must create course syllabi according to university and departmental policies, provide quality instruction, materials, feedback, and guidance to students, follow established institutional guidelines, and maintain a positive educational environment in the classroom. Compensation for each 3-credit-hour course is $3,200 for instructors with doctoral degrees, and $3,000 for instructors with master’s degrees. Qualifications Candidates must hold a master's degree in psychology. Previous teaching experience preferred. Required Attachments by Candidate Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Letters of Recommendation, Unofficial Transcripts, Teaching Philosophy or Statement All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 8f726d6f Last Name (required) 4bb2bb40 Email (required) cb7a64e3 Cell number 33d45fb5 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Ar